00:26:03.990 --> 00:26:05.689
What am I learning?

00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:09.684
I really appreciate this question,
I get asked it a lot.

00:26:09.684 --> 00:26:14.513
My own personal request is you
only need to add the amount

00:26:14.513 --> 00:26:18.018
of detail to let us know what is going on.

00:26:18.018 --> 00:26:22.342
I really appreciate that because you never
know who was reading on the other side and

00:26:22.342 --> 00:26:26.237
you want to be thoughtful to not
potentially trigger other experiences they

00:26:26.237 --> 00:26:27.440
might have had.

00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:31.750
So just be thoughtful, that goes for
the details that you're adding as well.

00:26:31.750 --> 00:26:36.720
Give us enough, so that we understand
the situation and then focus on you.

00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:40.790
What if my story is complicated?

00:26:40.790 --> 00:26:44.110
Sometimes this goes hand in
hand with these other pieces.

00:26:44.110 --> 00:26:48.330
The additional information
section can be your best friend.

00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:53.861
Maybe it is a term during college,
where you had extreme health crisis.

00:26:53.861 --> 00:26:56.626
Maybe it was something else
going on in your life.

00:26:56.626 --> 00:27:01.445
Maybe it is some of these extenuating
circumstances that inform you something

00:27:01.445 --> 00:27:06.492
that you've written, but don't necessarily
fit in with the flow that you have.

00:27:06.492 --> 00:27:10.965
Use that additional information space that
judiciously, but include any relevant

00:27:10.965 --> 00:27:16.300
bits of information that you think we need
to know, so that we really understand you.

00:27:16.300 --> 00:27:19.868
Bullet points are your friends here,
this is not additional essay,

00:27:19.868 --> 00:27:21.990
it's additional information.

00:27:21.990 --> 00:27:26.178
Be concise, again,
let us know what you think we need to,

00:27:26.178 --> 00:27:29.864
so that we really understand
your circumstances.

00:27:29.864 --> 00:27:32.310
How much explaining is
too much explaining?

00:27:32.310 --> 00:27:35.560
I kind of refer to this in some
of our previous responses.

00:27:35.560 --> 00:27:37.550
Am I learning more about you?

00:27:37.550 --> 00:27:40.020
Or am I learning about the situation?

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:42.680
In the holistic review process,
I want to know about you.

00:27:44.150 --> 00:27:46.290
And who will see my writing?

00:27:46.290 --> 00:27:51.940
So the admissions staff and you are the
only people who are going to see it.

00:27:51.940 --> 00:27:54.831
And whoever you share it with personally,

00:27:54.831 --> 00:27:59.900
we don't share this with faculty,
is not part of the evaluation process.

00:27:59.900 --> 00:28:02.989
We are trained professionals,
not even your alumni,

00:28:02.989 --> 00:28:05.520
interviewers are going to see it.

00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:09.223
All they see is your resume, and
you know exactly what goes on there.

00:28:09.223 --> 00:28:13.415
So know that this is a safe, confidential
space that if you do want to go somewhere

00:28:13.415 --> 00:28:17.674
vulnerable, or if you're talking about
something, maybe for the first time,

00:28:17.674 --> 00:28:21.305
if it's something that maybe
the world doesn't know about you, but

00:28:21.305 --> 00:28:23.402
you want to discuss it with us, you can.

00:28:23.402 --> 00:28:25.100
And we're not going to be
sharing that with anybody.

00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:28.540
Okay, so that was quick questions.

00:28:29.810 --> 00:28:31.000
How do I stand out from the crowd?

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.410
This is that next question
I get all the time.

00:28:33.410 --> 00:28:35.840
So center yourself,
I talked a lot about that.

00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:39.870
Embrace your journey and
be true to your reasons and rationale.

00:28:39.870 --> 00:28:44.137
Discuss the things that are meaningful
to you just if I had a quarter for

00:28:44.137 --> 00:28:47.983
every time I said the word you,
[LAUGH] in these presentations.

00:28:47.983 --> 00:28:51.429
Hopefully that's an indicator for
where we're going with like,

00:28:51.429 --> 00:28:55.750
what we're hoping we're getting out of
this journey with you, so and think deep.

00:28:57.140 --> 00:28:59.500
This is where those
interesting bits come out.

00:28:59.500 --> 00:29:02.452
This is where,
even if we all say something like family,

00:29:02.452 --> 00:29:04.173
the way we've engaged with it and

00:29:04.173 --> 00:29:07.570
your own experience with family is
going to be different from mine.

00:29:07.570 --> 00:29:10.580
It's going to be different
from everybody on this call.

00:29:10.580 --> 00:29:15.400
So really go there and understand
the whos and hows of what you are.

00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:17.872
So we're going to do a quick exercise.

00:29:17.872 --> 00:29:20.990
You might have done this with me before or
