to take it but remember, this is

00:47:48.574 --> 00:47:54.020
almost like a one page conversation
that we're having with each other.

00:47:54.020 --> 00:47:58.980
And you also want that person on the other
side to feel comfortable as they're

00:47:58.980 --> 00:48:02.260
reading yours so,
I would also use that as a plug for

00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:05.970
if I'm talking about
something controversial.

00:48:05.970 --> 00:48:10.528
Don't be controversial to get
a rise out of someone to get their

00:48:10.528 --> 00:48:15.430
attention it's about what am I
learning about you from this process

00:48:15.430 --> 00:48:20.590
hopefully that was helpful I know that
can be a kind of fine line to draw,

00:48:20.590 --> 00:48:23.692
but again trust your best judgment there.

00:48:23.692 --> 00:48:29.461
Question from Daniel from my exercise
is it more appropriate than your or

00:48:29.461 --> 00:48:32.336
should you be for primary job?

00:48:32.336 --> 00:48:36.063
So how much detail like when were
asking about what is your primary job

00:48:36.063 --> 00:48:37.920
responsibilities?

00:48:37.920 --> 00:48:42.318
That is one where I would say, we're
asking about your job responsibilities, so

00:48:42.318 --> 00:48:46.940
that could definitely be where you put
manages aquatic cultivation program?

00:48:46.940 --> 00:48:51.141
But in terms of like Blitz, I was more
referring to like bullet points on

00:48:51.141 --> 00:48:55.903
your resume, because that's where we want
to know what you did and even an impact

00:48:55.903 --> 00:49:00.340
questions read you got it right when
you're interpreting that question.

00:49:01.990 --> 00:49:02.611
All right?

00:49:02.611 --> 00:49:07.293
And then in terms of the process, and I
want to kind of come back to the holistic

00:49:07.293 --> 00:49:11.740
review process and I know that
this has been a recurring theme.

00:49:11.740 --> 00:49:16.417
It doesn't really matter which part of
the application we're reading first,

00:49:16.417 --> 00:49:21.372
because we're going to be looking at every
single piece of it together to understand

00:49:21.372 --> 00:49:25.582
who you are, no one part is that
gateway piece, not even an interview.

00:49:25.582 --> 00:49:26.160
Right?

00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:30.057
It can feel like sometimes the interview
was a make it or break it but

00:49:30.057 --> 00:49:33.886
that's not how it works we'll hear
back from the interviewer and

00:49:33.886 --> 00:49:38.270
then we'll look at that kind of report
in conjunction with everything that

00:49:38.270 --> 00:49:41.079
you submitted same goes for
this application.

00:49:41.079 --> 00:49:45.950
So if you think your way through it,
we want to know you threw it out so

00:49:45.950 --> 00:49:48.686
take yourself out from that mindset,

00:49:48.686 --> 00:49:53.729
take ownership of the things that you
can do here and please know that we

00:49:53.729 --> 00:49:59.222
are reading with your best intent in mind
we are reading to admit not to deny.

00:49:59.222 --> 00:50:03.759
And so with that, thank you so much for
joining us hopefully this was helpful,

00:50:03.759 --> 00:50:07.011
hopefully didn't inundate
you with too many details.

00:50:07.011 --> 00:50:10.651
If you have questions, we have many
more events both this week and

00:50:10.651 --> 00:50:14.885
throughout the summer above and feel
